<h1>Experiences</h1>
<p>An experience is an interactive kiosk presentation for a screen. Unlike playlists (which auto-advance through ads), experiences let visitors browse a listing on a touch screen — swiping through photos, viewing floor plans, and scanning a QR code to get more info on their phone.</p>

<h2>When to use an experience</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Open houses</strong> — Set up a tablet or TV at the entrance showing the featured listing</li>
  <li><strong>Lobby displays</strong> — A touch kiosk in the brokerage lobby for walk-in visitors</li>
  <li><strong>Window displays</strong> — A passive-looking display that becomes interactive when someone touches the screen</li>
</ul>

<h2>Creating an experience</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Go to <strong>Experiences</strong> and click <strong>New Experience</strong></li>
  <li>Give it a name (e.g., "350 Fifth Ave Open House")</li>
  <li>Select a listing — the experience will showcase this property</li>
  <li>Optionally assign a specific agent (otherwise the listing's primary agent is shown)</li>
  <li>Save the experience</li>
</ol>

<h2>What visitors see</h2>
<p>The experience displays on the screen as a full-screen property presentation:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Photo gallery</strong> — swipe or tap arrows to browse all listing photos</li>
  <li><strong>Property details</strong> — price, address, beds/baths/sqft, description</li>
  <li><strong>Agent card</strong> — the agent's photo, name, and contact info</li>
  <li><strong>QR code</strong> — visitors scan to open the listing on their phone</li>
  <li><strong>Floor plans</strong> — tap to view (if the listing has floor plans attached)</li>
</ul>

<h2>Idle mode</h2>
<p>After a period of no interaction (default: 30 seconds), the experience returns to an attract state — auto-advancing through photos to catch the next visitor's attention. Any touch restarts the interactive session.</p>

<h2>Assigning to a screen</h2>
<p>Assign an experience to a screen the same way you assign a playlist — go to the screen's page and choose the experience as the screen's content. A screen can have either a playlist or an experience, but not both at once.</p>
